{"explanation":"EncryptedKey.encrypt now creates a unique 96-bit nonce and explicit 128-bit-tag GCMParameterSpec for every AES/GCM encryption initialization. It preserves the public method signature by translating an unsupported explicit-parameter initialization into the existing InvalidKeyException contract, while retaining the existing AAD and Cipher-produced AlgorithmParameters behavior.","review_assumptions":["The Android versions/providers supported by this module provide javax.crypto.spec.GCMParameterSpec and accept a 96-bit nonce with a 128-bit authentication tag for AES/GCM/NoPadding. This should be confirmed against the module's minimum supported API level and target providers.","The existing retained AlgorithmParameters encoding remains the persisted encrypted-record representation; this edit changes only encryption initialization and leaves that representation and decrypt consumption unchanged."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"high","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","original_code":"import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
